AN1 Cc: Contact Person: Name: Christian Bergljung E-mail Address: Christian.Bergljung@ericsson.com Send any reply LS to: 3GPP Liaisons Coordinator, mailto:3GPPLiaison@etsi.org Attachments: None 1. Overall Description: With regard to enhanced information exchange between the UE and gNB to improve scheduling and network performance when using higher power CA/DC, RAN4 would like to provide the following recommendation and guidance as a follow-up to our earlier Reply LS in R4-2303701 from RAN4#106: RAN4 recommends the specification of a (reactive) information exchange based on existing PH and duty-cycle reporting amended with power-class fallback reporting (DPpowerclass) The definition of the corresponding PHR events is FFS can be combined with full-power MIMO transmission capability reporting corresponding to the current power class RAN4 was not able to agree on reporting P-MPR for FR1 with value ranges (similarly to the FR2 MPE-reporting with its 3 dB ranges) RAN4 stops the discussion on reporting prediction with specific evaluation periods and durations in Rel-18. RAN4 does not consider EHR feasible. RAN4 does not preclude prediction methods but consider the reactive information exchange described above a necessary baseline. 2. Actions: To RAN1 group. ACTION: RAN4 asks RAN1 to consider the above in its further work. 3. Date of Next RAN WG4 Meetings: 3GPPRAN4#108 21 – 25 August 2023 Toulouse, France

{"chunk_id":"R4-1905907-001","collection":"ran4_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Huawei"],"tdocNumber":"R4-1905907","title":"Capturing the IAB background"},"point_id":"3979138043327191776"}
ast meeting it was agreed that a new TS would be generated in RAN4 to capture the IAB node RF parameters, however there is currently no TR in the WID in which to capture any background. As it seems likely that a co-existence simulation campaign will be carried out, it will be useful to have somewhere to capture the results. In addition background for the RF parameters should be captured. Discussion Currently there are no new TR’s listed in the WID [1] to capture any of the WI technical details. It would seem that some point about the TR will be amended. However there are a number of choices for capturing the RAN4 specific work. A new RAN4 TR could be started The RAN4 technical analysis and co-existence study summary can be added to a larger TR for the whole WI The analysis could be added to existing TR for NR such as TR 38.817-2 No TR It is useful to capture the simulation scenarios and the results analysis in a TR. As there will be a new RAN4 TS to capture the IAB node RF requirements, it makes sense that there is an accompanying TR which capture the background behind that specification. For similar WI such as CLI, a RAN4 TR exists to capture the co-existence study results, and in that case there is no TS for new equipment only the analysis. Therefore a new TR to capture the RAN4 simulation work and RF background is preferable. Summary This paper briefly discussed the need for a RAN4 specific TR for IAB, and expresses our opinion that it is necessary. [1] RP-182882 New WID: Integrated Access and Backhaul for NR Qualcomm

